 "finding": "The published Sphinx tomogram reproduces with its author's code, unchanged, on its line and settings: the line's ends land within half a pixel of the pixels the KMZ states, and 7 of the 8 positions our run passes at a support of one stand in the published figure at the same places (9 there: [6, 9, 29, 30, 31, 51, 71, 77, 88]; ours [6, 9, 29, 31, 51, 71, 77, 86]). The published figure's support-two pair ([29, 30]) appears in our runs when the line moves by one pixel. Moving the line one pixel along track (4.6 cm) or across it (15 cm) keeps 3 to 6 of those 8 positions; the author's earlier East line, 2 to 15 m away, keeps 0; a motionless copy of the image, with nothing moving, passes 4 positions of its own; the 2025 pass passes 20, 3 of them shared. One line takes 30 s here."
